From e5091605d7000a19d43b2d67cbbd2c6be4defa47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:20:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: passthrough backend: the guest's own methods on the host
 GPU (EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_WORDS=1)

Each guest entry is decoded and copied into its host channel's pushbuffer with the host-class rewrites:
guest Ampere B classes bound as the Ada ones (plus inline-to-memory and 2D when RM has them), Tegra
syncpoint methods, firmware/software/instrumentation/zcull methods, the guest's ISA version and TLB mem
ops dropped, SET_SRGB_WRITE 0 (Ada sRGB-encodes UNORM targets with it), shader local memory moved to a
per-channel host buffer sized for the host's 72 TPC slots, report and semaphore operations at unmapped
VAs dropped (NVN releases to VA 0). Re-encoding keeps runs (encoder self-test at start).

Compute macro calls are replaced by the methods the split front emitted for them (OnComputeMacro/Emit;
the host MME writes inline QMDs one word late); OnStep keeps the pairing right for entries resumed after
an acquire. Inline QMDs go to host slots (Eglantine reads the guest's back). NVN's QMD dependence (barrier
QMDs scheduled with a count, raised/lowered by PCAS2 and by dependent QMDs) is tracked in stream order with
Eglantine's own rules (native_qmd.h); a barrier that reaches 0 is copied by the copy engine on the GPU
timeline (NVN patches its release payloads while it waits), its dependence cleared by semaphore AND
reductions, and launched there.

While Eglantine still executes every entry, it alone writes and waits on the guest's semaphores (two
writers deadlocked MKW; a host acquire behind Eglantine waited forever): EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_RELEASES=1
turns host releases and acquires on. An entry that ends inside a method run is held and submitted with its
continuation (a host MME left mid-call raised Xid 13 MISSING_MACRO_DATA). Program pages becoming or
changing as shadow pages wait for the host channels first (an unmap-then-map window gave Xid 13 Shader
Program Header). Ready() now honours EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH (the nvhost hooks opened an RM client without it).

Bisecting: EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_SYNC=1 (wait per entry), _DROP=<mask>, _WATCH=<va suffix>, _REREAD=1,
_SNAP=<s>:<va|0>:<size>:<file> (guest memory as the host GPU rendered it; 0 = the 2560x1440 sRGB output).

MKW: boots to the menu and race on the host GPU; the main menu read back from the output target is the
game's (ASTC textures black: not transcoded yet). No Xid in the last runs. Async mode still races
Eglantine's own memory writes (NVN's fence slots reset late): SYNC is the correct mode until the host is
the only executor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
